This adds `gh issue artifact delete` from #14527.

### Description

<!--
What's the problem? How are we addressing it?

Write for a reviewer who has not worked in this part of the codebase. Give them the
background they need before the problem makes sense, and avoid jargon.
-->

Issue artifacts are Markdown documents and links attached to an issue. The previous pull requests added the `gh issue artifact` command group, `list` and `view`. This one adds `delete`, which deletes artifacts by number. A deleted artifact can't be restored, so in a terminal gh asks first:

```text
$ gh issue artifact delete 142 2 5
! Deleted artifacts cannot be recovered.
? Delete artifacts 2 (OAuth callback plan) and 5 (Barista feedback notes) from monalisa/monas-cafe#142? Yes
✓ Deleted artifact 2 (OAuth callback plan) from monalisa/monas-cafe#142
✓ Deleted artifact 5 (Barista feedback notes) from monalisa/monas-cafe#142
```

- One prompt names every artifact, and its default is No. Declining deletes nothing and exits 2, like other gh prompts.
- `--yes` skips the prompt. Without a terminal, `--yes` is required, like `gh label delete`.
- Without `--yes`, a number that can't be found stops the command before the prompt, with `X Failed to delete artifact 9: Not Found` and `No artifacts were deleted.`
- With `--yes`, every number is attempted. Each artifact gets its own line, failures show the API's message, and any failure exits 1.
- Piped, each artifact gets one line with five tab-separated columns: status, number, name, source and reason. `delete` has no source, so that column is empty:

  ```text
  $ gh issue artifact delete 142 2 9 --yes | cat -t
  deleted^I2^IOAuth callback plan^I^I
  failed^I9^I^I^INot Found
  ```

- Like `list` and `view`, it refuses pull requests after one lookup and GitHub Enterprise Server before any artifact request. Types gh doesn't know are deleted as usual.

The [client](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/client/client.go#L116-L122) gains `Delete`. The [shared package](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/shared/results.go) gains the result lines, which the later commands in the stack reuse.

