### Key points

<!--
Tradeoffs you accepted, alternatives you rejected, and anything a reviewer would otherwise have to guess at.
-->

- **No artifact URLs yet.** #14527 also names artifacts by their URLs. The API doesn't return artifact URLs yet, as discussed in #14529, so `delete` takes an issue and numbers, and its help leaves URLs out. A later pull request in this stack will add them.
- **Every number is looked up first.** The prompt and the result lines name each artifact, so [`deleteRun`](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/delete/delete.go#L118-L155) gets every artifact before deleting any:

  ```go
  for _, number := range opts.ArtifactNumbers {
  	// The lookup gives the name, or the API's error
  	a, err := c.Get(repo, opts.IssueNumber, number)
  	...
  }

  if !opts.Confirmed {
  	// Without --yes, one failed lookup stops the command before the prompt
  	if slices.ContainsFunc(lookups, func(l lookup) bool { return l.err != nil }) {
  		...
  		fmt.Fprintln(opts.IO.ErrOut, "No artifacts were deleted.")
  		return cmdutil.SilentError
  	}
  	...
  	if !confirmed {
  		// Exits 2
  		return cmdutil.CancelError
  	}
  }
  ```

  With `--yes`, a number whose lookup fails gets a failed line, and gh sends no delete request for it. The other numbers are still deleted.
- **The result lines are shared.** `download`, `create` and `edit` report each artifact the same way, so [`PrintSuccess` and `PrintFailure`](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/shared/results.go#L30-L53) live in the shared package. In a terminal, successes go to stdout and failures to stderr, like `gh issue edit` with several issues. Piped, every line goes to stdout, like `gh pr checks` rows. The line already names the artifact, so its reason is only the API's message: `Not Found`, not `HTTP 404: Not Found (<url>)`.
- **Streams around the prompt.** The warning goes to stdout, before the prompt, like `gh issue delete` and `gh issue comment --delete-last`. `No artifacts were deleted.` goes to stderr, after the failed lines.
- **A repeated number isn't merged.** Each argument gets one line, so `delete 142 2 2 --yes` deletes artifact 2, then reports `Failed to delete artifact 2: Not Found`.

