Start with the [`delete` run function](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/delete/delete.go#L101-L178), which shows the order of the checks, the lookups, the prompt and the deletes. Then read the [shared result lines](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/shared/results.go). [`TestDeleteRun`](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/ea2fd6b15178c33ea3acf8ac6c50ecdce472f1f9/pkg/cmd/issue/artifact/delete/delete_test.go#L189-L594) has a row for each rule, including a failed lookup before the prompt, a failed delete after a lookup, a type gh doesn't know and a repeated number.

One detail isn't in #14527:

- #14527 shows prompts for one and two artifacts. With three or more, `delete` separates them with commas, including one before "and", like gh's other lists: `Delete artifacts 2 (OAuth callback plan), 3 (Staging OAuth runbook), and 5 (Barista feedback notes) from monalisa/monas-cafe#142?`

Related issues:

- #14527 is the `delete` design, with a screen for each scenario.
- #14529 is the RFC for the command group. Its discussion covers artifact URLs.

